# CSS Theming Rules

## MANDATORY: Use Only Defined CSS Variables

When styling components, you MUST use only the CSS variables defined in `app/globals.css`. Do NOT use hardcoded color values or create new CSS variables without updating globals.css first.

### Available CSS Variables

#### Background Colors
- `var(--color-bg-body)` - Main body background
- `var(--color-bg-surface)` - Surface background (slightly different from body)
- `var(--color-bg-card)` - Card/container background
- `var(--color-bg-hover)` - Hover state background
- `var(--color-bg-active)` - Active state background

#### Text Colors
- `var(--color-text-primary)` - Primary text color
- `var(--color-text-secondary)` - Secondary text color
- `var(--color-text-tertiary)` - Tertiary/muted text color
- `var(--color-text-inverse)` - Inverse text color (for colored backgrounds)

#### Border Colors
- `var(--color-border-primary)` - Primary border color
- `var(--color-border-secondary)` - Secondary border color
- `var(--color-border-focus)` - Focus state border color

#### Accent Colors
- `var(--color-accent-primary)` - Primary accent color
- `var(--color-accent-primary-hover)` - Primary accent hover state
- `var(--color-accent-secondary)` - Secondary accent color
- `var(--color-accent-success)` - Success state color
- `var(--color-accent-warning)` - Warning state color
- `var(--color-accent-error)` - Error state color

#### Border Radius
- `var(--border-radius-sm)` - Small border radius (0.375rem)
- `var(--border-radius-md)` - Medium border radius (0.5rem)
- `var(--border-radius-lg)` - Large border radius (0.75rem)
- `var(--border-radius-xl)` - Extra large border radius (1rem)

#### Shadows
- `var(--shadow-sm)` - Small shadow
- `var(--shadow-md)` - Medium shadow
- `var(--shadow-lg)` - Large shadow
- `var(--shadow-xl)` - Extra large shadow

#### Typography
- `var(--font-primary)` - Primary font family (Roboto)

### Usage Examples

```css
/* Correct - Using CSS variables */
.card {
  background-color: var(--color-bg-card);
  color: var(--color-text-primary);
  border: 1px solid var(--color-border-primary);
  border-radius: var(--border-radius-md);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
}

.button-primary {
  background-color: var(--color-accent-primary);
  color: var(--color-text-inverse);
  border-radius: var(--border-radius-sm);
}

.button-primary:hover {
  background-color: var(--color-accent-primary-hover);
}
```

```css
/* WRONG - Hardcoded values */
.card {
  background-color: #ffffff; /* ❌ Don't do this */
  color: #111827; /* ❌ Don't do this */
}
```

### Theme Switching

The application supports three themes:
- `light-mode` - Light theme (default)
- `dark-mode` - Dark theme
- `contrast-mode` - High contrast theme for accessibility (for users with visual impairments)

To switch themes, change the className on the `<html>` element in `app/layout.tsx`:
```tsx
<html lang="en" className="light-mode"> <!-- or "dark-mode" or "contrast-mode" -->
```

#### Contrast Mode Features
The contrast mode is specifically designed for users who have difficulty reading:
- Pure black (#000000) background
- Pure white (#ffffff) text
- High contrast borders (white on black)
- Bright, vibrant accent colors (cyan, yellow, magenta, pure green/red)
- Yellow focus indicators for maximum visibility
- Light shadows for depth perception

### Adding New Theme Variables

If you need new theme variables:
1. Add them to ALL theme sections (`.light-mode`, `.dark-mode`, and `.contrast-mode`) in `app/globals.css`
2. Use descriptive, semantic names following the existing pattern
3. Update this .cursorrules file with the new variable documentation

### Best Practices

1. Always use semantic variable names (what it is, not what it looks like)
2. Never use hardcoded colors, shadows, or border-radius values
3. Ensure all interactive elements have hover/active states using theme variables
4. Test components in all three modes (light, dark, and contrast)
5. When using Tailwind classes, prefer custom CSS with variables for theme-aware styling
6. Consider accessibility when designing UI - contrast mode should remain highly readable
